NebOS browser compatibility ladder
=================================

One page per behaviour.  Each failing page is a small, isolated test:

  left pane  (A) uses the feature under test
  right pane (B) produces the same result with primitives that already work

When the two panes look identical the feature is correct.  Later the panes can
be screenshotted and diffed automatically because they are at fixed offsets.

Serve this directory from the host and open it on the board:

  make compat-serve
  # or: python3 -m http.server -d testdata/browser/compat 8000

  browser http://<host>:8000/            # board
  browser http://10.0.2.2:8000/         # QEMU with -netdev user

Status: 010-029 pass.  Still missing from the ladder: table rowspan,
float text wrap/clear, @font-face, percentage margins/padding, and the
full CSS background/transform property sets (the pages cover the forms
that the engine implements).

Rules for new pages:
  - one behaviour per page;
  - no JavaScript and no network assets outside this directory;
  - explicit white background and dark text;
  - page chrome uses only primitives introduced earlier in the ladder;
  - keep the two panes at fixed offsets: floats with explicit px widths.
